# Asian Mushroom and Red Cabbage Stir-Fry

Based on [https://www.loveandlemons.com/stir-fry-recipe/](https://www.loveandlemons.com/stir-fry-recipe/)

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 2 Tbsp [Neutral Oil]{ ing="neutral-oil" }, divided
- [ ] 2 [Shallots]{ ing="shallots" }, thinly sliced
- [ ] 3 cloves [Garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, minced
- [ ] 1 Tbsp Fresh [Ginger]{ ing="ginger" }, grated
- [ ] 8 oz [Oyster Mushrooms]{ ing="oyster-mushrooms" }, torn into strips
- [ ] 1/2 head [Red Cabbage]{ ing="red-cabbage" }, thinly sliced (about 4-5 cups)
- [ ] 8 oz [Firm Tofu]{ ing="firm-tofu" }, pressed and cubed (optional)
- [ ] 3 Tbsp [Soy Sauce]{ ing="soy-sauce" } or Tamari
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [Rice Vinegar]{ ing="rice-vinegar" }
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [Brown Sugar]{ ing="brown-sugar" } or Maple Syrup
- [ ] 1 tsp [Sesame Oil]{ ing="sesame-oil" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [Red Pepper Flakes]{ ing="red-pepper-flakes" } (optional)
- [ ] 2 [Green Onions]{ ing="green-onions" }, thinly sliced
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [Sesame Seeds]{ ing="sesame-seeds" } for garnish

## Recipe

1. If using [tofu]{ ing="firm-tofu" }, press it for 15 minutes, then cube and pat dry
1. Heat 1 Tbsp [oil]{ ing="neutral-oil" } in a large skillet or wok over high heat
1. If using tofu, add it and cook 3-4 minutes per side until golden. Transfer to a plate
1. Add remaining 1 Tbsp oil to the skillet
1. Add sliced [shallots]{ ing="shallots" } and cook 2-3 minutes until softened and lightly caramelized
1. Add [garlic]{ ing="garlic" } and [ginger]{ ing="ginger" }, cook 30 seconds until fragrant
1. Add [oyster mushrooms]{ ing="oyster-mushrooms" } and cook 4-5 minutes without stirring initially to get a good sear, then toss occasionally until golden
1. Add sliced [red cabbage]{ ing="red-cabbage" } and stir-fry for 5-7 minutes until cabbage is tender but still has some bite
1. In a small bowl, whisk together [soy sauce]{ ing="soy-sauce" }, [rice vinegar]{ ing="rice-vinegar" }, [brown sugar]{ ing="brown-sugar" }, [sesame oil]{ ing="sesame-oil" }, and [red pepper flakes]{ ing="red-pepper-flakes" }
1. Pour sauce over the vegetables and toss to coat
1. Add tofu back to the skillet if using, and toss everything together
1. Cook for 1-2 minutes until sauce is absorbed and everything is heated through
1. Remove from heat and garnish with [green onions]{ ing="green-onions" } and [sesame seeds]{ ing="sesame-seeds" }
1. Serve immediately over rice or vermicelli noodles, or enjoy as a side dish

## Notes

- Tear oyster mushrooms by hand along their natural grain for the best texture
- Can substitute shiitake, cremini, or king oyster mushrooms
- High heat is key for a good stir-fry - don’t overcrowd the pan
- For extra protein without tofu, add edamame or cooked chicken
- Red cabbage will turn a vibrant purple-blue color when cooked
- Leftovers can be refrigerated for 3-4 days and reheated
